      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-319278",
      ":question/problem": "A bakery owner has at most $$450$ to purchase rice and flour. To qualify for a wholesale discount, she must buy at least $120$ kilograms in total. Standard rice costs $$2.90$ per kilogram and premium flour costs $$6.20$ per kilogram. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the maximum weight of premium flour the bakery owner can purchase while staying within the budget and keeping the discount?\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
