      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-319284",
      ":question/problem": "An orchard manager must keep a nutrient mix under $80$ cubic meters. To achieve target concentration, the total spend must be at least $$124$. Standard water costs $$0.90$ per cubic meter and nutrient solution costs $$3.60$ per cubic meter. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the minimum volume of nutrient solution the manager can include while meeting both constraints?\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
